  },
  {
   "id": 543018,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Packages must be loaded into freight cars to be transported by train. It is preferred to use the fewest freight cars possible to keep the costs down. As each freight car is packed, the package with the largest girth that will fit in the freight car is loaded and this is repeated until the freight car can hold no more packages. When a freight car can hold no more packages, the next freight car is loaded.",
